The Sealbreak maintainer, Georges Alkhouri, is aware that the terms of
service that apply to apps distributed via Apple's App Store services,
including TestFlight, may conflict with rights granted under the
Sealbreak license, the GNU General Public License, version 3. The
maintainer does not wish this conflict to prevent the
otherwise-compliant distribution of derived apps via the App Store or
TestFlight. Therefore, the maintainer has committed not to pursue any
license violation that results solely from the conflict between the
GNU GPLv3 and the Apple App Store or TestFlight terms of service. In
other words, as long as you comply with the GPL in all other respects,
including its requirements to provide users with source code and the
text of the license, the maintainer will not object to your
distribution of the Sealbreak app through the App Store or TestFlight.

This commitment applies only to code in which the maintainer holds the
copyright. It does not cover contributions whose copyright belongs to
other authors, or separately licensed third-party components.
